  "_README": "Golden set for the OPTIONAL skill-link suggestion (scripts/extract_claims.py, suggest_skill_links). Examples are referenced BY ID from eval/claim_prefill_labeled.json -- abstract, statement and topics live there and are not duplicated here. 'gold' is the skill link a reviewer would accept; an EMPTY list is a real label, not a gap: the catalogue is future-skills-shaped and most education studies legitimately map to no skill, so the empty cases are what measure whether the model holds back. LABELLING RULE: a claim links a skill only when it reports a MEASURED result about that skill. A position paper, recommendation or design description that argues for a skill without measuring anything is labelled EMPTY, however on-topic it reads — it is not evidence FOR the skill. Being merely adjacent to a skill's topic is also not enough. '_recorded' is the model suggestion last captured for the same prompt, filled by scripts/eval_skill_links.py --record-live. DO NOT wire these into data/ -- evaluation artifact only.",
